# CQ-26  For a failed trade, which backup trade replaced it and with which
#        seller?
# Group G (added in self-review v0.2). Basis: SHIFT-RR-08 (backup sellers and
# clearing logic).
#
# Parameters (method note 5): the trade status that triggers backup lookup.
#
# NOTE this returns nothing on the aran graph. The vocabulary is present and
# correctly shaped -- shift:backupTrade, domain shift:FlexibilityTrade, range
# shift:FlexibilityTrade -- and 41 trades carry status "Failed", but the v0.1.1
# generator asserts no backupTrade triple, so no failed trade reaches a
# replacement. The gold answer is empty too. Recorded as vacuous. The gap is in
# the ABox, not the vocabulary: RR-08 is one of the 22 rules with no executable
# SPARQL in this release.
PREFIX shift: <https://w3id.org/shift/core#>
PREFIX xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
SELECT ?failedTrade ?backupTrade ?backupSeller
WHERE {
  # -- parameters --------------------------------------------------------
  VALUES ?FAILED_STATUS { "Failed"^^xsd:string }   # RR-08 default
  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  ?failedTrade a shift:FlexibilityTrade ;
               shift:tradeStatus ?FAILED_STATUS ;
               shift:backupTrade ?backupTrade .
  ?backupTrade shift:sellerActor ?backupSeller .
}
ORDER BY ?failedTrade
